            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery-right ventricular fistula after coronary artery bypass grafting.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>155-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Development of a coronary artery fistula rarely occurs after cardiac surgery. We report the appearance of a coronary artery-right ventricular fistula as a consequence of coronary artery bypass grafting. Possible mechanisms and consequences are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
